     "text": [
      "<think>\n",
      "To find the cube root of 27, I can use the definition of a cube root, which means finding a number that when multiplied by itself three times equals the original number.\n",
      "\n",
      "I know that 3 multiplied by itself three times (3 × 3 × 3) equals 27. Therefore, the cube root of 27 is 3.\n",
      "</think>\n",
      "\n",
      "**Solution:**\n",
      "\n",
      "We are asked to find the **cube root** of **27**. \n",
      "\n",
      "The cube root of a number \\( x \\), denoted as \\( \\sqrt[3]{x} \\), is a number that when multiplied by itself three times (\\( y \\times y \\times y \\)) gives the original number \\( x \\).\n",
      "\n",
      "Mathematically,\n",
      "\\[\n",
      "y = \\sqrt[3]{27}\n",
      "\\]\n",
      "This means:\n",
      "\\[\n",
      "y \\times y \\times y = 27\n",
      "\\]\n",
      "\n",
      "Let's find such a \\( y \\):\n",
      "\\[\n",
      "3 \\times 3 \\times 3 = 9 \\times 3 = 27\n",
      "\\]\n",
      "So,\n",
      "\\[\n",
      "y = 3\n",
      "\\]\n",
      "\n",
      "**Final Answer:**\n",
      "\\[\n",
      "\\boxed{3}\n",
      "\\]"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "for chunk in llm.stream(\"What is the 3rd root of 27?\"):\n",
    "    print(chunk.content, end=\"\")"
   ]
  }
